    },
    {
      "title": "Comparisons and alternatives",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "When copies exist in every region of a multi-region cluster, Atlas can use faster direct-attach restores from local copies after a regional outage instead of slower cross-region streaming restores. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/backup/cloud-backup/snapshot-distribution/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:713413604e41cf4af3125cbacb555f65ae27caadb3b5e3c3d6e2ef1203b28458",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:64967aaa08bf25fe20d5068a45f951c3debff1b538fda4d248a70da10bfe680f",
            "ev:a7cf9347332532c2d5f2ab89bcab31db6188a7fceb87db0fcfc98c82e72b884f"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/architecture/current/disaster-recovery.md"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Atlas Cloud Backup stores snapshots in the cloud provider region of the cluster's current primary node by default. A snapshot copy policy distributes copies to additional regions; its policy items specify the target region, copy frequency, retention time, and whether to copy oplogs. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/backup/cloud-backup/snapshot-distribution/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:3d190f736b688e6edea7c454186c30fd1e4978031a0bb949534817c2d669d936",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:1bd0d0cdba021e287f0a7f74468ef5898f6cd127ebc8564cdf964d0765d9a4e9"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://github.com/mongodb/terraform-provider-mongodbatlas/blob/master/docs/resources/cloud_backup_schedule.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Point-in-time restore from a copy region requires Continuous Cloud Backup and oplog copying to that region. Oplog copying is enabled at the region level, so enabling it for one policy item makes point-in-time restore available for all snapshot-copy policies in that region. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/backup/cloud-backup/snapshot-distribution/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:6d55946a71eac72e36b4e791eac475145e84a7b39f59161a2c141b6ade8dda8c",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:8a4a152a8f73ee25a2f551c5f682b07670acf1fa2504315f7fb997649d664d13",
            "ev:8d7a0a19898cfa6b632b513a93e6212366e5c280d050b949b5974b6a0257ac35"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://github.com/mongodb/terraform-provider-mongodbatlas/blob/master/docs/resources/cloud_backup_schedule.md"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Atlas requires snapshot copy regions to use the same cloud provider as the cluster's primary region. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/backup/cloud-backup/snapshot-distribution/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:9708e348cd7c656a3b491311ea976e96362e7d1f6e118981afa9472f540d46f2",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:8eb1a409a820cd1722ac12334b9c0456b333c2c527a7b78520055985adec1d4d"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-03-31-mongodb-set-up-cross-region-backup-atlas/view"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The current Atlas snapshot-distribution documentation says the feature is not supported on Atlas Infinite clusters during public preview. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/backup/cloud-backup/snapshot-distribution/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:86984a2dd41357d518f15f48e06c59788c8df99d6dac0690d18a1151ddeab544",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:524c0ca8d6bcaf1384eefc34c5ad5436ff6ba96a5a1bb0ad9ab8760b27c28bb6",
            "ev:5908f1fa558a34364562c23814bc9e20d06a0b4418b8fbf0a0917e76c5db3aa1"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/infinite/atlas-infinite-landing/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MongoDB's February 17, 2026 announcement describes controls for selecting snapshots, setting copy retention independently from source snapshots, and applying policy changes to existing copies. The Terraform provider documents copy_policy_items or last_number_of_snapshots selection and update_copy_snapshots or delete_copy_snapshots controls. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23) Sources: https://www.mongodb.com/company/blog/product-release-announcements/introducing-enhanced-control-for-cross-region-snapshots ; https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/terraform-provider-mongodbatlas/master/docs/resources/cloud_backup_schedule.md",
          "source": "https://www.mongodb.com/company/blog/product-release-announcements/introducing-enhanced-control-for-cross-region-snapshots",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:b1d7fd37fc616390f20f58652edea6fdb1bf874279c962951195c7f89fd8e344",
          "validationStatus": "REMEDIATED-PROJECTION",
          "evidenceIds": [],
